<UnderConstruction/>

This is a guide for the internals of the `dir-structure` library.
After reading this, you should be able to understand a bit about how the
library works, and how to extend it. In this guide, we will be extending
it to support a new type of wrapper, `FsMtime`, which will allow us to
read and write the modification time of files.

<ScrollyCoding>

## !!steps Begin

Let's start by defining the wrapper type first.

```rust,no_run
use std::time::SystemTime;

use dir_structure::{DirStructure, DirStructureItem};

// !collapse(1:4)
// !mark(1:4)
struct FsMtime<T> {
    mtime: SystemTime,
    value: T,
}
```

## !!steps ReadFrom

Now, we need to implement the `ReadFrom` trait for our wrapper type.

```rust,no_run
use std::path::Path;
use std::time::SystemTime;

use dir_structure::{DirStructure, DirStructureItem, ReadFrom, Result};

// !collapse(1:4) collapsed
struct FsMtime<T> {
    mtime: SystemTime,
    value: T,
}

// !mark(1:5)
impl<T: ReadFrom> ReadFrom for FsMtime<T> {
    fn read_from(path: &Path) -> Result<Self> {
        todo!()
    }
}
```

## !!steps Metadata

Let's grab the metadata of the file and read the modification time.

```rust,no_run
use std::path::Path;
use std::time::SystemTime;

use dir_structure::{DirStructure, DirStructureItem, ReadFrom, Result, WrapIoError};

// !collapse(1:4) collapsed
struct FsMtime<T> {
    mtime: SystemTime,
    value: T,
}

impl<T: ReadFrom> ReadFrom for FsMtime<T> {
    fn read_from(path: &Path) -> Result<Self> {
        // !mark(1:3)
        let mtime =
            path.metadata().wrap_io_error_with(path)?
                .modified().wrap_io_error_with(path)?;
        todo!()
    }
}

```

## !!steps ReadFrom Value

Now, we need to read the inner value from the path.

```rust,no_run
use std::path::Path;
use std::time::SystemTime;

use dir_structure::{DirStructure, DirStructureItem, ReadFrom, Result, WrapIoError};

// !collapse(1:4) collapsed
struct FsMtime<T> {
    mtime: SystemTime,
    value: T,
}

impl<T: ReadFrom> ReadFrom for FsMtime<T> {
    fn read_from(path: &Path) -> Result<Self> {
        let mtime =
            path.metadata().wrap_io_error_with(path)?
                .modified().wrap_io_error_with(path)?;
        // !mark
        let value = T::read_from(path)?;
        todo!()
    }
}
```

## !!steps Return

Finally, we return the wrapper type with the modification time and the inner value.

```rust,no_run
use std::path::Path;
use std::time::SystemTime;

use dir_structure::{DirStructure, DirStructureItem, ReadFrom, Result, WrapIoError};

// !collapse(1:4) collapsed
struct FsMtime<T> {
    mtime: SystemTime,
    value: T,
}

// !collapse(1:9)
impl<T: ReadFrom> ReadFrom for FsMtime<T> {
    fn read_from(path: &Path) -> Result<Self> {
        let mtime =
            path.metadata().wrap_io_error_with(path)?
                .modified().wrap_io_error_with(path)?;
        let value = T::read_from(path)?;
        // !mark
        Ok(FsMtime { mtime, value })
    }
}
```

## !!steps WriteTo

Now, we need to implement the `WriteTo` trait for our wrapper type.

```rust,no_run
use std::path::Path;
use std::time::SystemTime;

use dir_structure::{DirStructure, DirStructureItem, ReadFrom, Result, WrapIoError, WriteTo};

// !collapse(1:4) collapsed
